<<~ ahu slot=`#/invocation`>>

!! Invocation Pattern

All masks enter a session via kahea transclusion in LARES:

```
<<~ kahea mask=`mask` uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/masks/SUBTYPE/MASK-NAME`>>
stage = 10
active = true
<<~/kahea>>
```

Named Voice masks may also be invoked directly by their earned name in Voice house notation.

!!! Entry and summon read as two acts

''Entry'' seats a mask for the session and declares the depth it stands at by default. ''Summon'' moves
a mask already seated, for as long as the moment asks:

```
<<~ stage rank=`20` name=`Mischief-Muse`>>
```

The depth rides first — a summon answers //how near// before //who// — and reads on the 0--20 stage
scale the boot seed declares by name (`green-room` · `offstage` · `upstage` · `center-stage` ·
`downstage`), with the fourth wall opening at 18 and above. A summon WEIGHTS surfacing and never
gates, so masks share the apron and no collision rule arbitrates them.

<<~/ahu>>

